dge support from our major funders, cite46†member institutions†info.arxiv.org , , and all contributors.\nL158: cite47†About†info.arxiv.org · cite48†Help†info.arxiv.org · cite49†Contact†info.arxiv.org · cite50†Subscribe†info.arxiv.org · cite51†Copyright†info.arxiv.org · cite52†Privacy†info.arxiv.org · cite53†Accessibility†info.arxiv.org · cite54†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org L159: \nL160: Major funding support from\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2511.09407v1] CARE-Bench: A Benchmark of Diverse Client Simulations Guided by Expert Principles for Evaluating LLMs in Psychological Counseling (https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.09407v1)\nciteturn5953view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.09407v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 158\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Computation and Language\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 12 Nov 2025]\nL9: # Title:CARE-Bench: A Benchmark of Diverse Client Simulations Guided by Expert Principles for Evaluating LLMs in Psychological Counseling\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Bichen Wang , cite6†Yixin Sun , cite7†Junzhe Wang , cite8†Hao Yang , cite9†Xing Fu , cite10†Yanyan Zhao , cite11†Si Wei , cite12†Shijin Wang , cite13†Bing Qin L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled CARE-Bench: A Benchmark of Diverse Client Simulations Guided by Expert Principles for Evaluating LLMs in Psychological Counseling, by Bichen Wang and 8 other authors\nL14: cite14†View PDF cite15†HTML (experimental) L15: > Abstract:The mismatch between the growing demand for psychological counseling and the limited availability of services has motivated research into the application of Large Language Models (LLMs) in this domain. Consequently, there is a need for a robust and unified benchmark to assess the counseling competence of various LLMs. Existing works, however, are limited by unprofessional client simulation, static question-and-answer evaluation formats, and unidimensional metrics.\nL16: These limitations hinder their effectiveness in assessing a model's comprehensive ability to handle diverse and complex clients. To address this gap, we introduce \\textbf{CARE-Bench}, a dynamic and interactive automated benchmark. It is built upon diverse client profiles derived from real-world counseling cases and simulated according to expert guidelines. CARE-Bench provides a multidimensional performance evaluation grounded in established psychological scales.\nL17: Using CARE-Bench, we evaluate several general-purpose LLMs and specialized counseling models, revealing their current limitations. In collaboration with psychologists, we conduct a detailed analysis of the reasons for LLMs' failures when interacting with clients of different types, which provides directions for developing more comprehensive, universal, and effective counseling models.\nL18: Subjects:  | Computation and Language (cs.CL)\nL19: Cite as:  | cite16†arXiv:2511.09407 [cs.CL]\nL20:    | (or cite17†arXiv:2511.09407v1 [cs.CL] for this version)\nL21:    | cite18†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2511.09407†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL22: ## Submission history\nL23: \nL24: From: Yixin Sun [cite19†view email ]\nL25: [v1] Wed, 12 Nov 2025 15:19:44 UTC (4,791 KB)\nL26: \nL27: Full-text links:\nL28: \nL29: ## Access Paper:\nL30: \nL31: View a PDF of the paper titled CARE-Bench: A Benchmark of Diverse Client Simulations Guided by Expert Principles for Evaluating LLMs in Psychological Counseling, by Bichen Wang and 8 other authors\nL32: \nL33:   * cite14†View PDF L34:   * cite15†HTML (experimental) L35:   * cite20†